WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:10.159
Jump, jump, jump, wait, say hello. That
program has five blocks, and one does nothing.

2
00:00:10.379 --> 00:00:15.905
Repeat 3 times, jump, say hello. Three
blocks, and the cat does exactly the same.

3
00:00:16.405 --> 00:00:21.235
Here is a program with five blocks:
jump, jump, jump, wait, say hello.

4
00:00:21.455 --> 00:00:26.238
The wait block does nothing here. It
is an unused command, so take it out.

5
00:00:26.458 --> 00:00:32.217
Jump, jump, jump is the same block three
times. Combine them into repeat 3 times, jump.

6
00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:38.009
Three blocks now. The cat jumps three
times and says hello, exactly as before.

7
00:00:38.229 --> 00:00:43.013
Shorter does not mean it does less.
It is easier to read and to change.

8
00:00:43.513 --> 00:00:48.807
The last program left the cat two squares
along, and bigger than it started.

9
00:00:49.027 --> 00:00:53.624
Run move right, then jump. The moves
are right, but the place is wrong.

10
00:00:53.844 --> 00:00:58.906
Put a go home block at the top. The
cat is back at the start, normal size.

11
00:00:59.126 --> 00:01:03.074
Now move right, jump ends where
it should, every single time.

12
00:01:03.294 --> 00:01:07.798
Putting things back to their starting
state is called initialisation.

13
00:01:08.298 --> 00:01:11.874
Sometimes the blocks are right
and only a number is wrong.

14
00:01:12.094 --> 00:01:18.921
The flower is at square 3. Move right
1, jump, move right 1 stops at square 2.

15
00:01:19.141 --> 00:01:24.435
Change the first number from 1 to 2.
Change one number, and nothing else.

16
00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:29.996
Run it again. Right 2, jump, right
1 stops at 3, right on the flower.

17
00:01:30.216 --> 00:01:34.488
No block moved. Only the number
inside one block changed.

18
00:01:34.988 --> 00:01:38.657
Testing is running a program
to see what it really does.

19
00:01:38.877 --> 00:01:42.638
Debugging is finding what went
wrong, and then fixing it.

20
00:01:42.858 --> 00:01:47.735
This one says repeat 3 times, spin,
say hello. We wanted three jumps.

21
00:01:47.955 --> 00:01:53.342
The repeat repeats a spin. That block
is the bug, so change spin to jump.

22
00:01:53.562 --> 00:01:58.995
Now run it again. A fix you have not
tested is a fix you do not know works.

23
00:01:59.495 --> 00:02:04.511
Your blocks have other names too.
Scratch is the program most schools use.

24
00:02:04.731 --> 00:02:11.000
Move right is move 10 steps. Jump is
change y by 50. Spin is turn 90 degrees.

25
00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:19.486
Go home is go to x: 0 y: 0. Repeat 3
times is repeat 3. Same jobs, real names.

26
00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:24.908
Some blocks hold a number you can change.
Move holds steps. Wait holds seconds.

27
00:02:25.128 --> 00:02:31.536
Set volume holds one too. Volume is
how loud a sound is, from 0 to 100.

28
00:02:32.036 --> 00:02:36.773
A tidy program has no unused block
and no duplicate left written out.

29
00:02:36.993 --> 00:02:43.309
Go home first: that is initialisation.
Then change one number inside a block.

30
00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:47.244
Test after every change you
make. The run is the test.
